# ============================================================
# Lesson 03 — while
#
# Keyword of this lesson: while
#
# Run it:
#     python3 juru.py examples/guide/03_while.jr
#
# while repeats a block as long as its condition stays true.
# Something inside the block must move the condition toward
# false — that is what makes the loop end.
# ============================================================

# A countdown: fuel falls by 1 every round, so it hits 0.
fuel = 5
while fuel > 0 {
    say("T-minus " + fuel)
    fuel = fuel - 1
}
say("Lift off!")

# The condition does not have to be about counting:
pocket = 1
while pocket < 100 {
    pocket = pocket * 2
}
say("pocket money: " + pocket)

# Read it out loud, like Python people do:
#   "while fuel is greater than 0, say T-minus fuel and burn one."
